  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In sulphur estimation. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>471</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of an organic compound gave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4439</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of barium sulphate. The percentage of sulphur in the compound is _______(Nearest Integer)</p><p>(Given: Atomic mass Ba: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>137</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>32</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>16</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi></math> )</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "42",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Molecular mass of Barium Sulphate(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>) =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>233</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo><mi>sulphur</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>233</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>&#160;weight of&#160;</mtext><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mtext>&#160;formed&#160;</mtext></mrow><mtext>&#160;weight of organic compound&#160;</mtext></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>233</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4439</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>471</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p>Nearest integer:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>42</mn></math></p>"
